    "updated_at": "2023-12-04T15:14:06Z",
    "body": "> I still think it's a spec issue, because https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/infrastructure.html#parsed-as-a-css-color-value says\r\n> \r\n> > If _color_ is [`currentcolor`](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#valdef-color-currentcolor), then:\r\n> \r\n> So it's not covering `currentcolor` nested inside `color-mix()`.\r\n\r\nAlso not covering `currentcolor` inside [relative color syntax](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-5/#relative-colors) which now has [a bunch of tests](https://wpt.fyi/results/css/css-color?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=relative-currentcolor)",
