    "created_at": "2024-09-06T02:37:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-09-06T02:37:43Z",
    "body": "@tabatkins, to be sure, [parse-color](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color-4/#parse-color) should also be able to handle values set through CSS variables, right?\r\n\r\nContext: Currently no browser seems to support that. https://jsfiddle.net/6p5zusag/\r\nOnly Firefox is able to resolve `currentColor` when `color` has been set to such a variable (but they're also the only ones able to resolve `currentColor` from somewhere else than a `style=\"color:...` HTML attribute...).",
